Subject: [PATCH] plugin/CLAUDE.md: rule for raw HTML tags in reply

reply renders Telegram HTML; entity-escaped tags print literally.

--- a/plugin/CLAUDE.md
+++ b/plugin/CLAUDE.md
@@ -24,6 +24,23 @@
 question and may lose formatting — call `reply` explicitly, do not rely on the
 fallback.
 
+## Formatting — pass RAW HTML tags, never entity-escape the tags
+
+`reply` renders `text` as **Telegram HTML** (parse_mode=HTML). Pass markup tags
+**raw**:
+
+```
+reply({ chat_id, text: "<b>bold</b> <i>italic</i> <code>x</code>" })   // ✓ renders
+```
+
+NEVER entity-escape the tags themselves — writing `&lt;b&gt;` instead of `<b>`
+makes Telegram print the literal characters `<b>` in the message. This is a
+recurring bug; do not repeat it.
+
+Escape `&`, `<`, `>` **only** when they are literal content, never when they are
+markup: `1 &lt; 2`, `Tom &amp; Jerry`. Supported tags: `b i u s code pre a`.
+When in doubt, send plain text with no tags — safer than broken markup.
+
 ## Public group / multichat chats
 
 For group/supergroup chats the channel **outbox** path delivers your final text
